{#- Per-stage end-summary banner (PLAN-locale-and-command-observability ADR-004/006).
    Appended to every stages/*.md.j2. The caller MUST set before {% include %}:
      summary_done     — one line: what this stage accomplished
      summary_artifact — primary output artifact path / description
      summary_next     — user-facing next step (a /hm:<stage> command or 'STOP')
    Required bare vars (no | default) so a stage that forgets a {% set %} fails render
    loud under StrictUndefined — absent-case guard, ADR-002. Renders in config.locale
    via the output_language directive. Self-skips under an active autoloop. The banner
    fires once per stage, so a fused (concatenated) workflow emits one per stage; the
    Codex workflow_skill delegates and carries none. is_codex-agnostic prose. -#}
## Stage summary — print before you STOP

Skip this banner entirely if `.hm-loop-active` exists at the project root (the
autoloop uses machine receipts, not prose). Otherwise emit it as your final output,
in the configured output language:

<!-- @hm:banner:end -->
